course: dictionary
lesson: 10864
title: Vicious and the vicious circle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vicious means cruel, violent or dangerous. «A vicious attack» is an attack meant to hurt someone badly. The word attack tells you this: an attack hurts people, so vicious adds the idea of cruelty.
explain: Vicious can also describe an animal that is likely to bite. «Keep away from a dog that growls» is good safety advice, because a growl is a warning that the dog may be vicious. Vicious can also describe weather or pain: «a vicious storm» or «a vicious headache» means very strong or severe.
explain: «A vicious circle» is a fixed phrase. It means a bad situation where one problem causes another, and that makes the first problem worse. Read the whole phrase as one idea, and look at the words around it for clues.
explain: Some other languages have a word like vicious too. In Russian, «zlyi» also means wicked or mean, so «zlyi pes» is a vicious dog, not a dog that is only angry for a minute.
fact: Vicious means cruel and wanting to hurt, or violent.
fact: «Vicious» can describe an animal that is dangerous and likely to bite or attack.
fact: «Vicious» can also mean very strong or severe, as in «a vicious storm».
fact: «A vicious circle» is a bad situation where one problem causes another that makes the first worse.
fact: In Russian, «zlyi» also means wicked or mean, so «zlyi pes» is a vicious dog.
exercise: «The vicious dog growled and showed its teeth.» What does vicious mean here? | Friendly and happy to play | *Dangerous and likely to bite | Very tired and sleepy | Quiet and shy
exercise: «The storm was so vicious that the boats stayed in the harbour.» What does vicious mean here? | Small and gentle | Cold and wet only | Bright and sunny | *Strong and severe
exercise: Lucy says, «I stay up late, so I am tired, so I sleep in and I am late. It's a vicious circle.» What does vicious circle mean? | A happy time with friends | A game played in a ring | A kind of shape with many sides | *A bad situation where one problem causes another that makes the first worse
test: «The villain launched a vicious attack on the town.» Which word is closest in meaning to vicious? | Gentle | Bright | *Cruel | Slow
test: «He had a vicious headache all day.» What does vicious mean here? | Very quiet | Very short | *Very strong and severe | Very happy
exam: Which phrase is a vicious circle? | A round ball kicked across the field | A circle of children playing a game | A bright red circle on the map | *Late nights make you tired, and tiredness makes you stay up later
